From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:46:51 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: hi846: Get the clock before checking link frequencies
 against it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The link frequencies are now worked out from the external clock rate,
but the probe checks them against the device tree before it gets the
clock. clk_get_rate() on a NULL clock is 0, so every mode's frequency
comes out as 0, none is found in the list, and the check passes
whatever the device tree says.

Get the clock first.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
index 0fc27545e..469fe725f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
@@ -2207,6 +2207,12 @@ static int hi846_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	if (!hi846)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	hi846->clock = devm_v4l2_sensor_clk_get(&client->dev, NULL);
+	if (IS_ERR(hi846->clock))
+		return dev_err_probe(&client->dev, PTR_ERR(hi846->clock),
+				     "failed to get clock: %pe\n",
+				     hi846->clock);
+
 	ret = hi846_parse_dt(hi846, &client->dev);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(&client->dev, "failed to check HW configuration: %d",
@@ -2214,12 +2220,6 @@ static int hi846_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-	hi846->clock = devm_v4l2_sensor_clk_get(&client->dev, NULL);
-	if (IS_ERR(hi846->clock))
-		return dev_err_probe(&client->dev, PTR_ERR(hi846->clock),
-				     "failed to get clock: %pe\n",
-				     hi846->clock);
-
 	for (i = 0; i < HI846_NUM_SUPPLIES; i++)
 		hi846->supplies[i].supply = hi846_supply_names[i];
 
